WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.556
IT and OT use many of the same technologies, but they serve different missions.

00:00:05.556 --> 00:00:08.673
Enterprise IT supports communication, business applications, identity, analytics,

00:00:08.673 --> 00:00:09.842
and data processing.

00:00:09.842 --> 00:00:13.349
OT supports the observation and control of physical operations.

00:00:13.349 --> 00:00:18.415
That difference changes how risk is evaluated and how security work is performed.

00:00:18.415 --> 00:00:21.922
IT systems are often refreshed on relatively short cycles.

00:00:21.922 --> 00:00:27.768
OT equipment may remain in service for decades because it is integrated with expensive machinery,

00:00:27.768 --> 00:00:31.275
certified processes, or infrastructure that cannot be replaced casually.

00:00:31.275 --> 00:00:37.120
Older controllers and workstations may use unsupported operating systems or protocols with little built-in security.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:41.017
Replacement may require engineering redesign, procurement, testing, and an outage.

00:00:41.017 --> 00:00:42.966
Patching also carries different constraints.

00:00:42.966 --> 00:00:47.642
An IT team may deploy updates during a routine maintenance window and

00:00:47.642 --> 00:00:50.759
recover a failed endpoint from a standard image.

00:00:50.759 --> 00:00:55.825
In OT, a change may require a planned shutdown, vendor participation, process testing,

00:00:55.825 --> 00:00:58.553
safety approval, and a verified rollback method.

00:00:58.553 --> 00:01:03.229
A controller reboot at the wrong time can interrupt production or leave

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.178
equipment in an undesirable state.

00:01:05.178 --> 00:01:07.126
Availability requirements can be strict,

00:01:07.126 --> 00:01:11.023
but “never touch the system” is not a security strategy.

00:01:11.023 --> 00:01:14.530
OT teams still need vulnerability management, access control, monitoring,

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:15.699
and lifecycle planning.

00:01:15.699 --> 00:01:18.817
The controls must be adapted to the process.

00:01:18.817 --> 00:01:21.934
Passive discovery may be preferable to aggressive scanning.

00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:25.831
Network containment may reduce risk while a patch awaits testing.

00:01:25.831 --> 00:01:28.949
Compensating controls need owners, evidence, and expiration criteria.

00:01:28.949 --> 00:01:33.625
IT assumptions should therefore be tested before they are applied to OT.

00:01:33.625 --> 00:01:35.183
Automated isolation, endpoint enforcement,

00:01:35.183 --> 00:01:38.301
or credential changes can have unexpected operational effects.

00:01:38.301 --> 00:01:42.588
At the same time, OT cannot remain disconnected from enterprise governance.

00:01:42.588 --> 00:01:46.874
Modern operations depend on remote support, analytics, vendors, and business systems.

00:01:46.874 --> 00:01:51.940
The strongest programs combine IT security expertise with engineering knowledge and operational authority.
